{
  "$comment": "genUI round 4 (catalog/style.json `backgroundGradient` radial + `backgroundImage`, docs in its $comment): the BOX BACKGROUNDS contract, hand-written. `validate` = validateStyle(style, {path: \"style\"}) (src/style.ts; Rust style_check::validate_style). `radial` = the shared radial geometry: R = the distance from the centre C = (x·w, y·h) to the FARTHEST corner (CSS `circle farthest-corner`), a sample [px, py, t] paints the stop colour at t = |P − C| / R (src/background.ts radialRadius/radialT; Rust style::radial_radius/radial_t; Swift + Kotlin their painters' own functions), 1e-4 tolerance. `picture` = where a picture lands: [x, y, w, h] in the box for `fit` cover|contain and the focal fractions (CSS background-size + background-position; Image's focal_bounds), src/background.ts pictureRect, Rust style::picture_rect, Swift + Kotlin their painters'. `visual` = a RESOLVED style (hex colours) → the painted `backgroundImage` / `backgroundGradient` the core hands every native (Rust style::visual serialised = the FFI `backgroundImageJson` / `backgroundGradientJson`; Swift + Kotlin parse those strings into their PaintStyle). `css` = the web node sheet's declarations (src/web/theme-css.ts declarations): the layers top first, the gradient, the scrim (`color-mix`), then `var(--xui-bgi, <placeholder>)` the renderer sets to the decoded picture's url.",
